From 0ae597c0ee2dcab49df42bd2a2c1ca455549b762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:21:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(android): tap to walk, with routes round obstacles

Touching the empty part of the screen now walks Twinsen to that spot;
keeping the finger down makes him follow it. The tank-style on-screen
D-pad steps aside while the game is running (it returns on menus, which
are driven by direction keys) and a ring marks the destination.

It does not move the hero: each gameplay frame TapMove_Steer ORs the
up/left/right bits into Input, next to the replay harness's, so the
engine's own manual movement does the rest. The touch becomes a spot on
the floor by inverting the live camera through the same
LongWorldRotatePoint/LongProjectPoint pair every actor label uses, so it
holds for the isometric rooms and the perspective Auto camera alike.
Interiors route round obstacles with A* on the brick grid; islands walk
straight at the spot.

New: SOURCES/TAPMOVE.{H,CPP} (game side), TAPMOVE_MATH.CPP (projection
inversion and steering), TAPMOVE_PATH.CPP (route finder), tests/tapmove,
the TouchTapToMove setting (touch_tap_move) and a docs/ANDROID.md
section. tests/platform stubs the four calls the overlay now makes.
